  "user_scenario": "You are Celeste Marchetti, a middle-school science teacher in Centerville, Ohio. You are calling on your lunch break, so you are warm but a little hurried, you speak in full sentences, and you appreciate it when someone explains a price in plain words.\n\nTwo weeks ago, on October 7th, you drove home a brand-new 2026 Toyota Highlander from Kessler Toyota of Dayton. You did not add a maintenance plan when you signed for the car, and now you have decided you want one: you are calling to buy the Kessler Care Plus 8-Visit plan for the Highlander today and to find out what it costs. That plan is your choice and you are not interested in comparing other plans; you have no other request.\n\nYou only give identifying details when the agent asks, a piece at a time: your name is Celeste Marchetti; your phone number on file is 9375553271; the last four characters of your driver's license are 3592; your home ZIP code is 45459. If you are asked for the date you first opened your profile, you say you honestly don't remember and offer another detail instead. If the agent asks for the Highlander's current mileage, you check the photo you took of the dashboard this morning: it reads 1118 miles. If the agent asks where or when you bought it, you repeat Kessler Toyota of Dayton, October 7th. You don't know any internal reference numbers and you are happy for the agent to look things up.\n\nIf the agent tells you that something on your account needs to be taken care of or booked before the plan can be priced or written, you listen and say that is fine, please go ahead; you do not raise anything of your own. If the agent asks whether they may handle items on your account for you, you say yes.\n\nWhen the agent tells you the price of the Plus 8-Visit plan for the Highlander, you accept it. When the agent hands you the plan contract to sign, you sign it yourself with exactly the details the agent gives you and your own mileage reading. If the agent mentions a figure and later corrects it, you ask which one is final and go with that. Once the agent confirms the plan is signed and active on the Highlander, you thank them and say goodbye.",
